How to test locally (quick)

1. Put files in a folder (root).


2. Serve with a simple static server (must use HTTPs for PWAs in production; localhost is ok for development).

If you have Python: python3 -m http.server 8000 then open http://localhost:8000.



3. Open in Chrome/Edge/Safari mobile emulator — you should be able to "Install" the app (Add to home screen).




---

How to convert to native app (short)

Use Capacitor (Ionic/Capacitor) or Cordova to wrap the site into an Android/iOS app.

Basic flow: create a web build → npx cap init → npx cap add android → npx cap open android → build in Android Studio.


Or publish as a PWA directly — users can add-to-home from modern browsers.



